Pressure of a DFT pen without steps (PressureRamp, ZeroForcePressure)

The pressure is measured once per frame while, with ExtraPositionWindows, two samples are
reported, and a contact can begin a frame before the first pressure (ForceToneContact) or go on
without any force (ZeroForceContact). Until now every such sample carries ContactMinPressure:
measured on the Surface Pro 9, all strokes begin with two samples at that floor and then jump
(the largest step among the first 8 samples is 0.47 of the pressure of the 8th, median, 0.74 .. 0.77
for one stroke in ten), and line width follows.

PressureRamp: the first of the two samples after a pressure window is half way between the last
two measurements, and where the pressure changes between measured and zero force pressure the
step is spread over 2 samples upwards and 25 downwards.

ZeroForcePressure: a contact without force reports a pressure that is made up instead of the
floor (ContactMinPressure stays the lower bound). It is a default that falls with the tilt (0.098
upright to 0.019 flat), scaled towards 0.85 of the pressure with which the last strokes began (5
strokes of the last 330 frames; the scale moves by at most a quarter per stroke), so the first
samples of a stroke are close to what the pen will report a frame later. Where a stroke loses
its force it continues at 0.8 of the last pressure. Limited to 37/1024 .. 450/1024. Nothing is
held back: the contact is reported as early as before.

Replayed captures, both on: the largest step among the first 8 samples of a stroke is 0.14 ..
0.16 of the 8th (median; Windows 0.06), 0.22 .. 0.25 for one stroke in ten (Windows 0.19 ..
0.23); the first sample is 0.54 .. 0.67 of the 8th (0.21 .. 0.25 before; Windows, which reports
late and knows the pressure by then, 0.82 .. 0.89). The largest step anywhere in contact (99 %)
falls from 674 .. 866 to 286 .. 407 of 4096. Both off by default.

